      <h1>Hyperactivity from First Principles</h1>
      <p class="lede">Most of modern computing is scar tissue from a 1945 bottleneck: flattening concurrent mathematical structure onto a sequential instruction tape, then layering cache coherence, garbage collectors, separate test suites, unverified compilers, and hand-edited documentation on top. <strong>Hyperactivity</strong> rebuilds the entire stack from one local degree-2 interaction law and one zero-postulate cubical kernel — where <em>proofs are live computational content</em> that execute, optimize, and verify everything from 7nm silicon to AI, chemistry, and bare-metal OS.</p>
